  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes `typecheck`. I did not run `vite build` or load the scene in a browser, so the render and the first-frame signal are untested.\n\n- **Instancing:** 8,000 trunks (`instances.cylinder`), 8,000 canopies (`instances.cone`) and 2,000 rocks (`instances.sphere`) are three instanced nodes, plus a 240×240 ground plane.\n- **Determinism:** one fixed-seed LCG places everything in a radius-75 disc, so the forest is identical on every load.\n- **Colour:** canopies get random green HSL colours, and rocks get grey-brown ones. Both use white base materials, because instance colours multiply the material colour.\n- **Light and fog:** one directional light casts shadows, and a hemisphere light fills it. The fog is `effects.fog` with `mode: \"exp\"` and density 0.004.\n- **Camera:** an orbit camera at [0, 85, 135] looking at [0, 4, 0], with `autoRotate` 0.08 rad/s, so the whole forest is in view.\n- **Rendering contract:** I pass `resize: false` to `createAuraApp` so it uses the existing 640×360 canvas as is. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set from the first `onFrame` callback after `await app.ready()`.\n\n",
